 # Pose tracker continuation — 2026-11-21
+
+## A1 completed: availability wording and mapping history
+
+Patch: `0013-tracking-availability-wording.patch`. Historical snapshot `8c141ad` maps `v3xmPAR` (Machine Seated Fly) and `CHpahtl` (Machine Seated Hip Abduction) to null/UNSUPPORTED. Current generated map supplies `chest_fly` and `hip_abduction`, respectively. Native allow path uses `canTrack(config)` plus `nativePattern`; browser uses the local-pattern fallback. Historical UI text: "Camera tracking is not ready for this exercise. You can still log it manually." It also unconditionally displayed "Allow camera access when asked. This tracking option requires an internet connection." for the unmapped/non-native branch. Permission is not read in either availability decision, so the same messages appeared with permission granted. This supports a mapping/UI explanation but does not establish the installed phone version or exclude a separate device permission issue.
+
+New unsupported text: "Tracking is not supported for this exercise. Manual logging is available." Camera-permission help is rendered only when tracking is allowed. Permission handling is unchanged. Current mapped exercises retain their local tracking routes and experimental labels. No camera-stack audit was performed.
+
+Tests: `rtk proxy npx vitest run shared/__tests__/trackingAvailability.spec.ts`: 3 passed. Replacing only the screen with its pre-fix working-tree version makes the UI regression assertion fail; log `patches/a1-before-test.log` (test helper restored the current file in finally). `rtk proxy npx tsc --noEmit -p frontend/tsconfig.json`: passed. No expectations were changed. This is a routing/configuration and source-contract test, not a real permission prompt or phone rendering test. Session stops after A1 as requested.
 
 All labels are provisional and unreviewed. No phone accuracy, deployment, or APK claims.
 
